e h_t=29 xor ((t mod2)*v). Hole-cell theorem forces fixed selector rank >= d-2. Adaptive guard ell=s_low xor (parity of zeros in high bits)*v. If ell!=29, pick a fixed original witness for ell; extension coefficients (1+high_i,high_i). If ell=29 and a high bit is1, take first such i and flip its first coefficient, use fixed witness for28. Remaining case is precisely hole. At most 63+t disjoint affine contexts, affine maps within each, construction polynomial in explicit family size; covers one witness per attained syndrome, not all witnesses. No all-decider lower bound. All 31 base nonempty subsets satisfy strict rank condition; each additional plane increases rank by independent coordinate and the all-new subset has common v, so strict condition preserved."}
